# A coupled run is a case (user request 2026-10-20): flow-over-heated-plate opens from Cases with its own pages (Overview,
# Coupling setup, Participants, Run), a participant opens as a case with the way back, running a participant alone is
# refused (it would wait for its partners), and the coupled run goes with real buoyantPimpleFoam + laplacianFoam through
# preCICE (max-time cut to 0.05 s: five time windows).
shell sed -i 's|<max-time value="1" />|<max-time value="0.05" />|' $SB/ws/fohp/flow-over-heated-plate/precice-config.xml
click nav:cases
wait-until page Cases
wait 10
assert text flow-over-heated-plate
assert text 2 participants
open $SB/ws/fohp/flow-over-heated-plate
wait 10
assert text Temperature
assert text Heat-Flux
assert text serial-implicit: time windows of 0.01 up to t = 0.05
screenshot $OUT/cpl_overview.png
click nav:coupling setup
wait 10
assert widget cpl-set-tabs#1
click nav:participants
wait 10
assert text Interface1: mesh Fluid-Mesh on patches (interface)
click cpl-part-open#0
wait-until page Overview timeout 10
assert text fluid-openfoam
click nav:run
wait-until page Run
assert text is the Fluid participant of a preCICE coupling
click run-go
wait 5
assert toast alone it would wait for its partners
assert job idle
screenshot $OUT/cpl_participant_run.png
click run-cpl-parent
wait 10
assert widget cpl-go
click cpl-go
wait-until toast Started 2 participants timeout 20
wait-until toast Coupled run finished timeout 400
assert log fluid-openfoam/log.Fluid End
assert log solid-openfoam/log.Solid End
assert file fluid-openfoam/precice-Fluid-iterations.log
screenshot $OUT/cpl_done.png
